{"repositoryId":644081097,"availability":"available","full":"netlify/plugin-csp-nonce","name":"plugin-csp-nonce","description":"Build plugin to use a nonce for the script-src directive of your site's Content Security Policy.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":9,"forks":15,"created":"2023-05-22T19:19:55Z","updated":"2026-02-26T15:14:54Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://csp-nonce.netlify.app","topics":["csp","netlify","security"],"demo":"https://csp-nonce.netlify.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T15:44:35.491Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T15:44:35.491Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T15:44:35.491Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T00:56:38.156Z","stars":9,"forks":15},{"at":"2026-10-18T15:44:35.491Z","stars":9,"forks":15}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Use a nonce for the script-src directive of your Content Security Policy (CSP) to help prevent cross-site scripting (XSS) attacks.","This plugin deploys an edge function that adds a response header and transforms the HTML response body to contain a unique nonce on every request, along with an optional function to log CSP violations.","Scripts that do not contain a matching nonce attribute, or that were not created from a trusted script (see strict-dynamic), will not be allowed to run."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/netlify/plugin-csp-nonce/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f01b1e42c0272944861169a410a8b3aa32f62a552103efa513c6c7ff3fedd17e","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T00:56:38.253Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T00:56:38.253Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Use a nonce for the script-src directive of your Content Security Policy (CSP) to help prevent cross-site scripting (XSS) attacks.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/netlify/plugin-csp-nonce/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f01b1e42c0272944861169a410a8b3aa32f62a552103efa513c6c7ff3fedd17e","sourceUrl":"https://g